      "summary": "D3' locally closed carving (campaign :305). ADVANCED, NOT CLOSED. Owner released.\n\nWHAT PIC-E LANDED (run 0095 r5, Picard/DivSupportQuasiFinite.lean, 20 declarations, 0 sorries, rooted, lake build 8695 jobs EXIT=0, all axiom-clean [propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound] vs fgaPicardRepresentability firing sorryAx).\n\nTHE ROW'S BINDER IS REPRICED. Every theorem of Picard/DivPushforwardFlat.lean carries LocallyQuasiFinite (schematicSupportI x.F followed by pullback.snd pi T.hom), which that file calls producerless and not derivable from DivFamily's other fields. All still true. What is new: the binder is EQUIVALENT to finiteness of the fibres of D over T, because BOTH other binders mathlib's criteria want (LocallyOfFiniteType, QuasiCompact) come from DivFamily.properSupport -- LocallyOfFiniteType is a structure PARENT of IsProper, so it is a field access, not a search. At a family the producer's hypothesis list is one item. Names: DivFamily.locallyQuasiFinite_iff_finite_fibers, locallyQuasiFinite_iff_isFinite_fiber, locallyQuasiFinite_of_fibers, isFinite_support, isFinite_support_of_fibers.\n\nTRAP for anyone consuming those theorems: HasProperSupport is a def, NOT a class. 'haveI := hps' registers nothing and infer_instance fails on both free binders. Cite the named theorems.\n\nWHAT REMAINS, and it is TWO obligations not one -- corrected after a fresh-context audit refuted pic-e's own 'nothing between the antecedent and finiteness is unbuilt':\n (a) THE GEOMETRY: a nonempty effective Cartier divisor on a relative curve has finite fibres. On C_t, D_t is the zero scheme of a regular section of an invertible ideal on a 1-dimensional scheme. Untouched.\n (b) A CARRIER BRIDGE nobody had named: the fibrewise antecedent quantifies over the FIBRE OF THE SUPPORT, while DivDegree.lean's fibre SES (fiberCokernelIso, Scheme.DivFamily.isLocallyTrivial_fiber_kernel, mono_fiber_kernel_ii, fiberKernelIso) is about the SUPPORT OF THE FIBRE. rfl FAILS between the carriers, and the bridge is absent from the project: QuotSupportBaseChange.lean proves only annihilator F <= (annihilator of the pullback).map, the direction giving properness of the LARGER support. The reverse inclusion is what identifying the carriers needs.\n (c) D3' PROPER, unchanged: the ExistsUnique statement about the Grassmannian locus. Nothing above touches it. Also unchanged: the phi=id instance is not the antecedent as a FAMILY over all test phi -- settle which D3' needs before pricing inputs as done.\n\nDO NOT re-count the value. pic-e's commit messages claimed this retires plumbing for THREE rows; that was withdrawn. D4' consumes D3' and never binds LocallyQuasiFinite, so it was double-counted. HasLocallyConstantDivDeg (DivDegree.lean) names TWO inputs -- the B3 rank half PLUS quasi-finiteness -- and this supplies at most the second.\n\nDO NOT read the producer as content. DivFamily.locallyQuasiFinite_zero discharges the binder at DivFamily.zero for arbitrary pi and T, but the empty divisor is exactly where fibre finiteness is free, and MEASURED: with only the pre-existing isEmpty_schematicSupport_of_isZero in scope, plain infer_instance already closed both LocallyQuasiFinite and IsFinite there. It is satisfiability, and the file adds a name rather than access.\n\nSTILL TRUE from the earlier row text: DivFamily has exactly one producer in AJC (DivFamily.zero, Picard/DivFamilyZero.lean), so every Cluster D' theorem is testable at one family only. NOTHING HERE CLOSES THE SEAM SORRY; rep has no producer.",
